[2026-08-04T12:54:50.249Z] [safeoutputs] recv: {"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":3,"method":"tools/call","params":{"name":"create_pull_request","arguments":{"body":"Updates the \"Histograms in delta temporality only\" limitation in `docs/reference/compatibility/limitations.md`, which stated a blanket delta-only restriction for histograms. The restriction has been renamed and scoped: both delta and cumulative temporality are now supported for histograms and counters via the Elasticsearch OTLP endpoint (`motlp`) on Elastic Stack 9.5+ and serverless, while the collector's Elasticsearch exporter path still only supports delta temporality for histograms.\n\n**Triage rationale:** The issue provided clear before/after technical claims (what changed, the caveat that the collector exporter path is unaffected, and the exact section/lines to update), verifiable against the linked `docs-content://manage-data/ingest/otlp-endpoint.md#metric-temporality` page referenced elsewhere in this same file. This made the change sufficiently specified for autonomous handling without needing to guess at unstated product behavior.\n\n**Drafting sources**\n- Elastic Docs Contribution guide and cumulative-docs/`applies_to` guidelines (fetched conceptually via repository conventions; existing `applies_to` usage in `docs/reference/compatibility/limitations.md` frontmatter and other pages in `docs/reference/compatibility/`)\n- Existing published page: `docs/reference/compatibility/limitations.md` (source of the change)\n- Linked implementation/reference: `docs-content://manage-data/ingest/otlp-endpoint.md#metric-temporality` (Metric temporality docs referenced in the issue)\n- Issue #648 body, including the specific proposed wording, line range, and applies_to guidance from the reporter\n\n**Reader test**\n- Reader goal: an Elastic Observability user configuring OTel metric ingestion, determining whether cumulative-temporality histograms/counters are supported and what's required, depending on ingestion path (ES OTLP endpoint vs. collector ES exporter).\n- Rounds: 2\n- Round 1 found one blocking gap: the draft didn't clarify that the collector-exporter delta-only restriction never applied to counters, only histograms, which could have left readers uncertain about counter behavior on that path.\n- Round 2 (after adding \"This restriction doesn't apply to counters.\"): no blocking comprehension gaps remained.\n\nRelated to #648\n\nThis draft PR was produced autonomously by docs-agent-experimental in experimental mode.\n\nSafe-output PRs do not trigger CI by default. A maintainer must trigger the required checks manually.","branch":"docs-agent/issue-648-histogram-temporality","title":"Scope histogram delta-temporality limitation to collector Elasticsearch exporter"}}}
